			<div class="content" id="post-content-1527618">
									

<blockquote>
<p>The subject is rapidly altered, physically and biologically, with tissue samples harvested from subjects during medical exploration indicating this process extends down to a genetic level.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence is really awkward and could be better written perhaps as two separate sentences or at least a semicolon used.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Once transformed the subject is to all intents and purposes biologically dead.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'to all intents and purposes' seems off to me, this may just be me though.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Accordingly, subjects under the influence of SCP-1418 should be considered active biohazards.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This should be in the Containment Procedures, or at least noted somewhere in there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a high-society concern known to traffick in anomalous objects and which has been classified as a Group of Interest to the Foundation</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't believe this is particularly necessary, because there's a group of interest page people can check out if they don't know what MC&amp;D is.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>she was reported to have been dead for 4 weeks when discovered owing to the condition of her body</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm confused, do you mean 'she was reported to have been dead for approximately 4 weeks according to the condition of the body'? Or something? I don't understand. Maybe because I'm tired.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Due to Lady ████████ 's high profile and connections to the peerage an official inquest, which failed to record a cause of death, and a public auction of her assets was permitted.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Cutting down the 'which failed to record&#8230;' sentence, this sentence confuses me. 'Due to Lady XXXX's high profile and connections to the peerage an official inquest and a public auction of her assets was permitted'. This sentence just makes little sense to me, since the flow (afaik) should be 'Due to X and X, this happened'.</p>
<p>Both internal memos confuse me as to why they need to be there. I don't think they're telling me anything about the article, so why are these internal memos here? Are they supposed to hint an addictive nature or something?</p>
<p>Overall, neutral vote.</p>

							</div>

